=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">StockTok ETF Continues to run away from the S&amp;P 500</figcaption></figure></div><p>Before I cover that stock, the overall market continues to look fine. We covered this last week…nothing too concerning with S&amp;P 500 futures or the Russell 2000. The VIX has been relatively choppy…but nothing to cause alarm (for now). For the Gold, Silver and Bitcoin crowd out there (thank goodness we sold our silver stocks last Thursday…literally dodged a silver bullet lol)…<strong>DO NOT FIGHT TRENDS</strong>. I got dozens of “I am buying the dip” comments on my silver follow up video. The bitcoin maxis buy every red candle all the way to the bottom. Those individuals are now down another -6.4%, in a single day. Buying dips and dollar cost averaging down only sets you up for failure. You may get lucky a few times, but I have seen it over and over again, people EVENUTALLY blow up their portfolios.<em><strong> Don’t do it. </strong></em></p><p>Keeping this brief, I like to see how the market behaves on Monday’s before posting more analysis. </p><h4>Without further ado, the stock I am purchasing is: </h4>",
